-0.0680877 9.57134 -0.0140806 9.88529 0.212865 10.0456L7.00408 14.8432L4.40172 22.6166C4.35092 22.7683 4.37534 22.9352 4.46749 23.066C4.6275 23.2932 4.94137 23.3476 5.16853 23.1876L12 18.3758L18.8317 23.183C18.9625 23.2751 19.1293 23.2994 19.281 23.2486C19.5445 23.1604 19.6865 22.8752 19.5983 22.6117L16.996 14.8432L23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></defs><use clip-path="url(#clip_RatingStar_undefined-2small)" href="#path_RatingStar_undefined-2small" class="RatingStar__backgroundFill"></use><path class="RatingStar__fill"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/5601551119">January 3, 2024</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">➥ 2.5 Stars *:･ﾟ✧<br /><br /><blockquote><b>“I bet you say that to everyone you’re with,” she said.<br />Clutching her hips, I planted a kiss beside her navel.<br />“I’ve been alive too long to speak idly,” I said. “I’ve uttered those words to no one else.”</b><br /><br />━━━━━━━━━━━ ♡ ━━━━━━━━━━━</blockquote><br /><br />Honestly, I'd be surprised if I don't get kicked off Harley's ARC team 😭. For one, because I've been (outrageously) late with my mediocre-ass whiney reviews. But to that I say... maybe it's because your book (that I wanted so badly to love and hype up!) was boring!<br /><br />Now, it's so full of sweethearts on this site — people who motivate me to continue writing reviews — so here I am putting one out! Granted, I wish it could be a passionate, glowing review where I'd practically place your next read in your lap because of how I sold it, but sadly, that is <b>
  <u>not</u>
</b> the energy I can bring to the table today. There is a little sass though, so hopefully it'll be entertaining. Or! Sometimes the things I dislike in books are things that others seek so maybe my review won't be completely futile.<br /><br />Let's start with the not-so-bad. Harley Laroux's writing is, in my opinion, pretty fuckin commendable. I just think she describes what needs to be described, creates atmosphere and writes pretty natural and swoony dialogue. It's why I grew to love her work in the first place, because <i>frankly</i> dark romance is <b>
  <u>not</u>
</b> the genre to go to in hopes of good writing, in my (decent) experience. No shade to other dark romance authors but Harley is doing something right that many of you have just failed to (*cough* H.D. Carlton and Giana Darling etc.).<br /><br />Another one of her strengths is that she <u>adds to the genre</u>. Sure, she'll play with some tropes but to be, she stands out for a number of reasons.<br /><br />1) Her MMCs are pretty fuckin slutty and yet...so respectful. I know I know, we're not supposed to be in awe about these things nowadays but listen. She somehow nails the middle ground where there are fun, unique dynamics at play, yet with full consent, safety and generally just lovingness. These men really just love their girls and you can tell. Harley always confidently ticks that box for me.<br /><br />2) This one is gonna have a little shade in it but... I've grown to love Harley's fmcs, because in the previous sequel, we met the absolute gem of a woman: Juniper. This woman was hot, relatable and just oh-so-human. I want to see some sass, some grit in the FMCs of dark romance. It makes it so much more interesting when they're just as playful and teasing. And who doesn't love a power couple? But sadly, that was <b>
  <u>not</u>
</b> the case for this book.<br /><br />Listen, maybe it's bc of how utterly homo I am, but I was <b>
  <u>READY</u>
</b> to meet THE <b>Everly (h)</b>. The setup of this book was TOO GOOD man. We were promised a sexually dominant woman and I was <b>here for it</b>. But <b>"it" didn't get the memo</b>.<br /><br />Everly was meant to be this sickeningly, powerful witch who, yes, had her support pup (<b>Callumn (H)</b>) at her feet... but what did I get?<br /><br />I get one of the meekest, most clueless and stuttery fmcs to date!! 😭😭😭<br /><br /><b>BUT GET THIS</b> she STILL tries to be dominant in bed 🤣🤣🤣. Listen, I'm not gonna yuck anyone's yum or however that goes, (bc ofc people can be dominant in bed and not irl and vice verse), but as a READER there was a complete tonal shift that just <b>did not work</b> in favour of the character Harley was trying to create.<br /><br />Moreover, it was blatantly obvious that Callumn was just <i>letting her</i> try out sexual dominance, and though he seemed to enjoy his submissive role too, it took almost all the agency and like...zest from Everly's dominance in the first place. Like he literally had to guide her through her own domination of him I'm SORRY?!? Like...I get how it's a ...healthy... way for her to explore her sexuality but goddamn what was I even reading.<br /><br />It was never giving power couple, I was never swooning or giggling or twirling my hair for either character... it was just a mess.<br /><br />What I'd argue is best is when a character's personality matches their actions. Everly just had no bite in her man, it was <b>
  <u>boring!!!</u>
</b><br /><br />To elaborate (☝ lol), there was also a complete lack of the general push and pull dynamic that Harley always nails like what?!? I mean, I'd rather they didn't read my review because I would be heartbroken to have a reader so disappointed in my latest work that I pride myself in but gosh. I gotta get it out, sorry bae.<br /><br />There was no tension, no will-they-won't-they, it was all just <b>
  <i>"we're friends yippee now let's fuck but this time I peg you and you stick to your puppy eyes meanwhile i'm literally Bambi so what now"</i>
</b>. Because it just didn't make sense I'm SORRY.<br /><br />Because of that, it didn't really feel like there was much romantic development at all? It is so drilled into the reader that Callumn perceives Everly as being so naive and yet supposedly also like his divine powerful woman but...who's really buying it? Hand me a coupon because I CAN'T.<br /><br />Not to mention that I knew the plot would be repetitive but damn it just really lost its spark by the 3rd time witnessing the same plot from a different perspective.<br /><br />Holistically, I regret to report that this book failed on many fronts. I mean I just <i>still</i> cannot believe we were robbed of a powerful female witch, exuding elegance and commanding respect, that toyed with Callumn — THAT'S what I had signed up for, personally.<br /><br />By the end, it didn't feel like a love story and that's what Harley's other books have achieved (at least for me) in the past (the first two in this series).<br /><br />But unfortunately, I don't know what's in the air, or Harley's air for that matter, but her recent releases have left me somewhat stumped and entirely disappointed (the Losers duet etc). I keep feeling inclined to the "but the next one's premise is so good, it'll be GREAT and I'll be back on the Harley Hype Train" but that what I though about this one...<br /><br />And yet still! I <b>know</b> that Harley has a 🚨🚨🚨 SAPPHIC RELEASE 🚨🚨🚨 planned, and I'm so ready for her to NAIL a tryst-six-venom-esque toxic lesbian romance but I'm hesitant to even get too excited for it.<br /><br />Still, I do look forward to seeing her take on it, as I truly do believe she has the potential to publish a DELICIOUS sapphic romance, however, this one left such a bad taste in my mouth (dnfed at 88%) that I'm literally setting it as "read" on December 31st, 2023 because I just <i>don't</i> want to start the new year like this.<br /><br />Gosh, I hate to call a woman pathetic but Everly's meek and pouty character was not it for me, and Callumn wasn't anything special either.<br /><br />I've decided to still place one of the better quotes as the featured one for my review because like I said, it's not all bad, but it's just nothing in comparison to what I've seen Harley be capable of.<br /><br />Onto a new year and many more reviews! <br /><br /><i>Thank you Harley Laroux for an ARC of this book in exchange for an honest review!</i><br /><br /><blockquote>━━━━━━━━━━━ ♡ ━━━━━━━━━━━</blockquote></span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/126364621?shelf=arcs-or-review-copy" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">arcs-or-review-copy</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/126364621?shelf=online-tbr" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">online-tbr</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/126364621?shelf=romance-bdsm" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">romance-bdsm</span></a></span><span tabindex="-1"></span> <div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium" aria-label="Show all items in the list"><span class="Button__labelItem">...more</span></button></div></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContainer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">55 likes</span></button></div><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">6 comments</span></button></div></div><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><bu