kick myself for putting off the last book in this series, and wow… I was right. What a conclusion to a seriously underrated series.<br /><br />Of course it’s spicy. Of course it’s a demon romance. But can we take a second to appreciate the plot? Harley is brilliant. The way they wove this seamless story across all three books, overlapping scenes, different POVs, tiny details coming full circle it’s genius. I kept catching myself saying, “oh my God, I loved this part in book one” or “wait, this moment was so good in book two” and now I get to see it all play out. That’s the kind of storytelling that makes a series unforgettable.<br /><br />And the setting? Witches, gods, monsters, a creepy cult-filled town worshipping an evil god, it’s everything. Then there’s Everly, the outcast of her family, secretly one of the most powerful witches alive. Enter Callum, a literal archdemon who storms into her life to worship her, protect her, kill for her, and somehow be everything she needs. Their dynamic might be one of my favorite ever. I still can’t believe how soft this “big bad” demon is for her. He’s supposed to be terrifying, but he’s also playful, smirking, filling his coffee with five sugar cubes and a ton of cream, playing the piano beautifully (air piano included) and THE SNAPPING🤭🤭<br /><br />The way he hunts and taunts her, wakes from a two-decade coma, sees bruises on her arm and immediately says “who did this to you” so he can kill them I fear that’s my type. Their banter is chef’s kiss. She tells him he should wear a bell so he stops sneaking up on her and he’s like:<br /><br />“Like the ones humans put on their cats? Only if you promise to drag me around on a leash. I’ll gladly wear your collar.”<br /><br />I died. THE SIMP OF ALL SIMPS<br /><br />But what I love most is how he builds her up. He makes Everly strong, confident, reveling in every display of her power. “You are far more powerful than you have ever been allowed to believe.”<br /><br />This love feels bigger than them, like it’s something ancient and unshakable. I felt it deep in my bones.<br /><br />The ending was perfect, sometimes coming to the last book in a series that I love can be a little nerve-racking because I want it to be wrapped up properly and this one gave me everything I needed. The pacing was perfect and it didn’t feel rushed. That final moment that loops us back to the beginning almost killed me in the best way. This was the perfect conclusion to an incredible series, and I already want to re-read it just to catch all the details I missed the first time. I don’t think people appreciate how well-rounded this series is, and I really think it has the ultimate plot spice combination. I’m going to miss these characters so much. <br /><br /><br /><br /><br /><br /><br />“Home is wherever I can keep you safe.” 😭<br /><br /><br />“Thank you for giving me peace.”😭😭<br /><br /><br />“I make you mad. Tell me. Yell at me if you wish. Take your anger out if you need me, but don’t run from me. Face me, teach me, let me learn how to take care of you.” 😭😭😭<br /><br /></span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContainer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">51 likes</span></button></div></div><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review unliked. Press to like review"><span class="Button__labelItem"><i class="Icon LikeIcon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14.4813282,6.41129383 L14.586127,6.97676447 C14.5964421,7.03541935 14.6071117,7.09675198 14.6181364,7.1607667 L14.8551301,8.60363442 L17.440983,8.