40806 9.88529 0.212865 10.0456L7.00408 14.8432L4.40172 22.6166C4.35092 22.7683 4.37534 22.9352 4.46749 23.066C4.6275 23.2932 4.94137 23.3476 5.16853 23.1876L12 18.3758L18.8317 23.183C18.9625 23.2751 19.1293 23.2994 19.281 23.2486C19.5445 23.1604 19.6865 22.8752 19.5983 22.6117L16.996 14.8432L23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/5647584248">August 27, 2023</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">So glad to get back to this world and wrap up this story. I was swooning, gasping, covering my eyes, and thrilled the whole time.<br /><br />Everly is a character I have been curious about since the beginning. I knew more was going on with her, even when it was hard to feel for her at the beginning. She is stuck in a cult she wants nothing to do with but sees no escape. She has been brainwashed and mistreated and told she is next to useless.<br /><br />Then... something happens that pushes her over the edge and frees her from the clutches of her demented father. She discovers a magical house with a demon inside who tells her she can kill the creature she has been forced to worship.<br /><br />Callum is that demon and he has been patiently waiting for Everly to find him. He is there to help her take control of her powers and fight the evil looking to consume everything. But he's not just here for that.. he's also here for HER. He's been waiting so long and now that he has her... he'd let the world burn to keep her.<br /><br />I could not put this book down. I was obsessed with Everly and Callum right from the start. She has been through so much and it was hard to read about how she was treated and see the hopelessness of her situation. Watching her come into her magic and seeing her lose the chains that held her down was thrilling.<br /><br />That magic house in the woods was EVERYTHING! I loved the creatures and ghosts we met, the magic I saw Everly learn, and of course... the experimenting Callum coaxes her into... (see the steamy content warnings for a tease at that).<br /><br />I was a bit nervous after how long we waited for this conclusion to the trilogy but Harley Laroux delivered 100% for me. And I actually want to start from the beginning again to see how it all fits together. It came together so beautifully and I loved the cameos of all our previous faves.<br /><br />I highly recommend this whole trilogy and I think it only got stronger with each entry. I can't wait to see what the author writes next.<br /><br /><br />5 stars<br />5 on the spice scale<br /><br />TW: Abusive parent, death of a parent, torture, cult activity, discussion of pregnancy loss, body horror, and other horror elements, consensual drug use during sex<br /><br />Sexy CW: bondage, impact play, public play, blood play, knife play, lots of fluids, piercing play, monster cock, pegging and more</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/14949982?shelf=arcs-2023" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">arcs-2023</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/14949982?shelf=bdsm-recs" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">bdsm-recs</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/14949982?shelf=read-2023" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">read-2023</span></a></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__stat