br />Some of the spooky moments were truly scary and gross. And I mean that in the best way possible. This book opened the Spooky Season for me. We’re officially in Halloween Mode in this house all thanks to Harley Laroux. <br /><br />I’ve been waiting for so long to get to know these characters and it was even better than I could’ve anticipated. Even the rest of the characters, from her dead grandma who speaks to her through an old radio, to the Fae creatures… The magic house that anticipates all your needs. You know you’re getting old when you find yourself wanting that house above anything else lol<br /><br />Everly is an amazing FMC. She went through so much, and we got to see her growing and learning to use her magic until she became the powerful witch we already knew.<br /><br />I’m as obsessed with Callum as he was with Evelyn. And that’s A LOT. He was such an amazing character, I can’t stop thinking about him.<br /><br />Their sex dynamics were incredible. Again, Laroux delivers a different view on sex that just fascinates me. Her BDSM and sex scenes come closer to real life than most books. And that’s one of the reasons her books are so good. Without spoilers, I’ll say Callum's approach to pleasure and pain was so hot. He’s the ultimate Switch Daddy and I wish we got more of this because 😮‍💨<br /><br />The conclusion with the God, and all the discussion about what Gods were and how they managed to gain power was so interesting and satisfying. <br /><br />I’m sad this is the last book in this universe but I’m content with the way it ended. I can’t wait for what Laroux has in store for us next.<br /><br />ARC review</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/3587456?shelf=fave-male-main-character" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">fave-male-main-character</span></a><span tabinde