g to the point — my thoughts. I’ll start with the positive sides here.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eCallum, aka the Archdemon, Elder Warrior of the Onyx Stone Order, Defender of the High City, Prince of the Nine Circles, guardian of House Laverne and Magni Deicide. As you can see, he has quite a lot of titles, just as he has a lot of good, even amazing qualities. I liked this man, okay. He had one preference that I hate in my heroes, but he was endearing enough for me to overlook it and finish the book. Which is rare, as usually if a character doesn’t have issues with such things, it leads to me putting the book down. \u003cb\u003eSo, what made me love him?\u003c/b\u003e \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis nicknames.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cblockquote\u003e\n  \u003ci\u003e\n    \u003cb\u003e\"lady witch.\"\u003cbr\u003e\"my lady\"\u003cbr\u003e“My beautiful thread of fate. My lady. My mistress.”\u003cbr\u003e\"darling.\"\u003cbr\u003e“Yes, my love.\"\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/b\u003e\n  \u003c/i\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ \u003cimg src=\"https://images.gr-assets.com/hostedimages/1693740193ra/34680807.gif\" width=\"280\" height=\"180\" alt=\"description\" class=\"gr-hostedUserImg\" loading=\"lazy\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eUgh, he had a way with words. I know \"my lady\" might sound like something out of a historical romance novel, but I can't help loving it.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cblockquote\u003e\n  \u003ci\u003e\n    \u003cb\u003e“You should wear a bell so you don’t give me a heart attack.” \u003cbr\u003e“A bell? Like the one’s humans put on their cats?” He tipped his head to the side curiously, seeming to give the idea some thought. “Only if you promise to drag me around on a leash. Then I’ll gladly wear your collar.”\u003c/b\u003e\n  \u003c/i\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e*SCREAMINGGGGG*\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cblockquote\u003e\n  \u003ci\u003e\n    \u003cb\u003e“I don’t understand your anger,” I said. “Would you have preferred she penetrate me instead?” \u003cbr\u003eWhispered curses floated through the air. “It certainly would have been preferable.” \u003cbr\u003eThat was fair enough. I still didn’t understand, but humans worked in mysterious ways. \u003cbr\u003e“Well then, we’ll try that next time.” The explosion of cursing that followed my declaration told me perhaps I should stop talking entirely.\"\u003c/b\u003e\n  \u003c/i\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHe was effortlessly funny, and the best part was that he was completely serious here. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cblockquote\u003e\n  \u003ci\u003e\n    \u003cb\u003e\"Everly is not, and has never been, a mere fascination. She is my reason, my logic. She is my one and only God. Think I’m mad if you wish. There is nothing left for me in this existence except for her, and I would sooner rip myself apart than allow you or any other being to stand in her way.\"\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e“I’ll love you endlessly, darling.”\u003c/b\u003e\n  \u003c/i\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e'Darling' always does it for me.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cblockquote\u003e\n  \u003ci\u003e\n    \u003cb\u003e“I would build a temple for you if I could,” I said, dragging my nose along her skin as I inhaled. “Lock you away like a gilded goddess and worship at your feet for eternity.”\u003c/b\u003e\n  \u003c/i\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ \u003cimg src=\"https://images.gr-assets.com/hostedimages/1680758828ra/34114087.gif\" width=\"280\" height=\"180\" alt=\"description\" class=\"gr-hostedUserImg\" loading=\"lazy\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHe was obsessed. Honestly, even the word 'obsessed' feels like an understatement. At first, I was confused when, after just a few minutes of meeting her, he jumped straight to, \"Who f*cking hurt you? Give me their name.\", but it all made sense once he revealed why he knew who she was. He had been searching for her for centuries — long before she was even born. He had a vision of her, something nearly impossible for demons, where she begged for his help, and that vision drove him to Earth to find her. Imagine your man waiting for you for centuries — a new standard. He even threatened Lucifer himself and was ready to betray Hell for her.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eNow, onto my main issue — sharing. The moment a hero expresses any desire to share the heroine, it's an instant DNF for me. I know this might not bother everyone, but it's something I personally can't stand. I prefer heroes who are so possessive that they would never let another man near you. Don’t get me wrong — there isn’t a single scene like that in this book, but Callum does mention that it wouldn't be a problem for him.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cblockquote\u003e\n  \u003ci\u003e\n    \u003cb\u003e“I thought you weren’t the jealous type.” \u003cbr\u003e“Oh, certainly not, love. I’m very welcoming and generous to guests. It’s intruders I have a problem with.”\u003c/b\u003e\n  \u003c/i\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThen he started talking about other men \"helping him\" while he fuck*d her. While I understand that this might not be a problem for everyone, it’s something I personally dislike. I liked Callum enough to continue, but it did leave a bitter taste.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eOur heroine, Everly, is next. While I liked her, I didn't feel a strong connection to her character. She was portrayed as a powerful witch learning to control her magic, yet at the same time, she came across as sweet and shy. She was also a virgin who enjoyed reading smutty books. Through her relationship with Callum, she discovered a dominant side in the bedroom, and although I’m completely obsessed with dominant women, the moment she suddenly started talking dirty to him, it somehow caught me off guard.. One moment she was sweet, and then suddenly, \"Do you really want it that bad? Such a needy boy.\" I couldn't quite picture it — I don’t know why but, it felt out of character.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAs for the smutty scenes, I have to admit that I enjoyed them, some even a lot. But certain phrases, like 'my puckered hole,' were just a big no for me. I'm sorry, but it’s probably the worst possible way you can describe that.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe second thing that made me lower my rating is that I found myself a bit bored. It’s not that nothing was happening, but usually, I can finish a book of this length in a day—this one took me three.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIn the end, I'll just say that while I enjoyed certain aspects of this book, would I recommend it to anyone overall? Unfortunately, no. I wish I could, though.","rating":3,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1SUM3DHQFV3T\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.xGzgQB5fkrWMYEan\"}}"},"likeCount":208,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":31},"User:149414829":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":149414829,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1753217872i/149414829._UX200_CR0,77,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":325,"textReviewsCount":155,"name":"April ","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/149414829-april","contributor":null,"id":149414829},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1E6M8WGOVZYBC":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1E6M8WGOVZYBC"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1E6M8WGOVZYBC\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.xGzgQB5fkrWMYEan\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1E6M8WGOVZYBC","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1E6M8WGOVZYBC"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.xGzgQB5fkrWMYEan","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.xGzgQB5fkrWMYEan"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/149414829?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/5886132659"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.TPqyvyY-542YKK9cT6nzZw":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.TPqyvyY-542YKK9cT6nzZw","creator":{"__ref":"User:149414829"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1777945153766,"createdAt":1696413636300,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1701005626933,"text":"\u003cb\u003e“You are far more powerful than you have ever been allowed to believe.”\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThis series hooked me in from the beginning. The second book fell a bit for me, but this one reeled me right back in. I wanted some witchy vibes for the spooky season, and that is exactly what I got. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eA Soul for a Witch is the final book in the Souls Trilogy. It is an age gap, touch her and die, insta-love (but I didn't hate it), dark romance with witty banter, sarcasm, dirty talk, and magic. There are some plot crossovers since it's along the same timeline as the first two books, but we get more building and a backstory with this one before it crosses plots than we did with the second book. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eEverly Hadleigh bares witness to the murder of a fellow classmate by her half-brother to be sacrificed. She doesn't want to be caught up in it and ends up teleporting to a mysterious house deep in the woods. A house that she finds out holds magic and has housed her ancestors. What she finds there is the archdemon Callum, who had been waiting for her for 2000 years. Together, they want to kill the God in Abelaum. The first step of their plan is for Everly to return home to steal the grimoire from her father. When she returns home, she finds out from her father that the God will need a vessel that is filled with power and a mind with faith. Her father's plan is for her body to become its vessel. Will her and Callum be able to defeat the God together without being killed themselves, or Everly becoming the vessel?\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eFor so long, you haunted me. The familiar face of a stranger in a hundred lifetimes. As if we were always circling each other, two planets in cosmic alignment, thrown into a continuous loop by the power of one another. I waited for you, before I even knew it was you I was waiting for.\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAt the coven house, we meet Everly's grandmother, who is a ghost that speaks through a radio. I enjoyed her wisdom and funny and snarky remarks. We don't see much of the previous couples. All that we got was a scene of each, which made me kind of sad because I would have loved to see more of Leon. I was happy, though, not to see much of Victoria and Jeremiah as I don't like either of them.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e“I do miss you,” I mumbled against her neck. “Miss you every second I’m not touching you. Every moment I can’t see you.”\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThis may have started as insta-love, but their relationship grew into much more. We see the building of their relationship until their chemistry is explosive. They are literal soulmates. I loved Callum with his sarcasm, witty comebacks, and his obsession with Everly was top tier. And oh my gosh, the nicknames that he gave Everly made me swoon so hard. You guys he read one of her romance novels and planned a picnic for her. I need a Callum lol. Gosh Everly, I loved her so much! She was a sweet, shy girl who was always told that she was weak. Well, let me tell you, she grew into a strong, confident witch and learned how to master her magic. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e“I love you,” I said. “I love you more than life itself, more than my own freedom. For you and you alone, I’ve stayed alive, Everly. For you, I would face everything I ever feared. I’ve lived a thousand lifetimes and I swear I’ve loved you in every one of them.”\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI have been enraptured by this world and am sad that the series has come to an end. And what an ending it was. I was scared for both Callum and Everly sitting on the edge of my seat with what would happen next. I loved the epilogue it was sweet and heartwarming. Please check out the triggers before picking this up. I can't wait to see what else Harley has in store for us and to read others that I haven't yet. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e“To whom do you belong, my demon?” “To you, darling. You will have me in life. I will keep you in death. For eternity, I am yours, and you are mine.”\u003c/b\u003e","rating":4,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1E6M8WGOVZYBC\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.xGzgQB5fkrWMYEan\"}}"},"likeCount":163,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":67},"User:151685472":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":151685472,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1685882033i/151685472._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":885,"textReviewsCount":557,"name":"Noa","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/151685472-noa","contributor":null,"id":151685472},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A2A7WAJ7JTZP07":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A2A7WAJ7JTZP07"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A2A7WAJ7JTZP07\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.xGzgQB5fkrWMYEan\"}}":{"_