m as I'm a slut for harley laroux and the books she writes","rating":0,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1ZRJJNRZZPRS4\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.xGzgQB5fkrWMYEan\"}}"},"likeCount":52,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":12},"User:155283672":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":155283672,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1755706215i/155283672._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":1721,"textReviewsCount":307,"name":"Brittany Ferraro","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/155283672-brittany-ferraro","contributor":null,"id":155283672},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A368TJKYH9QI1V":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A368TJKYH9QI1V"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A368TJKYH9QI1V\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.xGzgQB5fkrWMYEan\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A368TJKYH9QI1V","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A368TJKYH9QI1V"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.xGzgQB5fkrWMYEan","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.xGzgQB5fkrWMYEan"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/155283672?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/5824059784"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.AZ3RCWFUc1LzVQLmjI4Yyg":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.AZ3RCWFUc1LzVQLmjI4Yyg","creator":{"__ref":"User:155283672"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1778119481805,"createdAt":1759366001854,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1759374612227,"text":"I knew I was going to kick myself for putting off the last book in this series, and wow… I was right. What a conclusion to a seriously underrated series.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eOf course it’s spicy. Of course it’s a demon romance. But can we take a second to appreciate the plot? Harley is brilliant. The way they wove this seamless story across all three books, overlapping scenes, different POVs, tiny details coming full circle it’s genius. I kept catching myself saying, “oh my God, I loved this part in book one” or “wait, this moment was so good in book two” and now I get to see it all play out. That’s the kind of storytelling that makes a series unforgettable.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAnd the setting? Witches, gods, monsters, a creepy cult-filled town worshipping an evil god, it’s everything. Then there’s Everly, the outcast of her family, secretly one of the most powerful witches alive. Enter Callum, a literal archdemon who storms into her life to worship her, protect her, kill for her, and somehow be everything she needs. Their dynamic might be one of my favorite ever. I still can’t believe how soft this “big bad” demon is for her. He’s supposed to be terrifying, but he’s also playful, smirking, filling his coffee with five sugar cubes and a ton of cream, playing the piano beautifully (air piano included) and THE SNAPPING🤭🤭\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe way he hunts and taunts her, wakes from a two-decade coma, sees bruises on her arm and immediately says “who did this to you” so he can kill them I fear that’s my type. Their banter is chef’s kiss. She tells him he should wear a bell so he stops sneaking up on her and he’s like:\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e“Like the ones humans put on their cats? Only if you promise to drag me around on a leash. I’ll gladly wear your collar.”\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI died. THE SIMP OF ALL SIMPS\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eBut what I love most is how he builds her up. He makes Everly strong, confident, reveling in every display of her power. “You are far more powerful than you have ever been allowed to believe.”\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThis love feels bigger than them, like it’s something ancient and unshakable. I felt it deep in my bones.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe ending was perfect, sometimes coming to the last book in a series that I love can be a little nerve-racking because I want it to be wrapped up properly and this one gave me everything I needed. The pacing was perfect and it didn’t feel rushed. That final moment that loops us back to the beginning almost killed me in the best way. This was the perfect conclusion to an incredible series, and I already want to re-read it just to catch all the details I missed the first time. I don’t think people appreciate how well-rounded this series is, and I really think it has the ultimate plot spice combination. I’m going to miss these characters so much. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e“Home is wherever I can keep you safe.” 😭\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e“Thank you for giving me peace.”😭😭\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e“I make you mad. Tell me. Yell at me if you wish. Take your anger out if you need me, but don’t run from me. Face me, teach me, let me learn how to take care of you.” 😭😭😭\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A368TJKYH9QI1V\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.xGzgQB5fkrWMYEan\"}}"},"likeCount":51,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:147485288":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":147485288,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1785192162i/147485288._UY200_CR2,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":151,"textReviewsCount":456,"name":"Ash","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/147485288-ash","contributor":null,"id":147485288},"User:kca://pro