},"likeCount":33,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":8},"User:126482905":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":126482905,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1770574343i/126482905._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":7,"textReviewsCount":283,"name":"Jennifer","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/126482905-jennifer","contributor":null,"id":126482905},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/AEILDFRP3W1EX":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/AEILDFRP3W1EX"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/AEILDFRP3W1EX\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.xGzgQB5fkrWMYEan\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/AEILDFRP3W1EX","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/AEILDFRP3W1EX"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.xGzgQB5fkrWMYEan","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.xGzgQB5fkrWMYEan"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/126482905?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/5817984402"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.SFYYyWaYsILNZS2HWB1Szw":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.SFYYyWaYsILNZS2HWB1Szw","creator":{"__ref":"User:126482905"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1781550971187,"createdAt":1694749092376,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1694750531357,"text":"This is the hardest thing I have ever had to do. Because I love this author and I loved book 1. And so many of their other books. But I will not lie. And I will piss some people off but this was one of the worst books I have ever read. Book 2 was meh but this? \u003cbr /\u003eI am confused. I feel punked. Did I read the wrong book? \u003cbr /\u003eThis has to have been a first draft? Right?! As my most anticipated book in two years I am heartbroken. \u003cbr /\u003eIf you don’t want spoilers please go but just know this hurts me a lot to do. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003ePlot: the plot was thready at best, mostly consisting of a odd bunch of tropes, non triggers but triggers and a bunch of plot lines that never connected. First why did we have to go over the same story line all over again? This read as a standalone but with vital pieces of the other books. It was redundant and by far 70% of this book didn’t need to be written. It was all filler. Which leads me to my next issue. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe writing: This DID NOT feel like this authors prior works. This was a first draft. Full of unnecessary information, descriptions with minimal dialogue. This was 90% tell no show. I felt nothing, no fear, no disgust, nothing that the author was attempting to portray but fell flat on. Which is a 180 from book 1. When you constantly had to describe the movements, the room or the outfit it was too much. Over kill. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe character’s: fuck. Everly and Callum were my most anticipated couple book. I was wet waiting for them. But they lacked connection. Tension. All of it was just words. Once again no show only tell. Everly is a young virgin new witch who happens to become a dom, mistress and the most powerful witch of all? That is so not okay. And here is Callum, we see this badass scary demon in the prior books and in this one he is a bottom, which I love, but he turns into a total baby. He lacks a spine and changes like after ch 11. Their sex was so cringe, he couldn’t even fit in her the first time but by the third time he’s bottoming out to the point her stomach is bulging? Oh let’s not forget the second time they even have relations she pegs him which damn I’m so good for but you are telling me this virgin is able to do all this? Come on. Oh the best part they mark each other and pierce each other and after being the dom she begins pulling out a “fuck me like a whore” wait what. I’m 70% in where the heck did this come from. They lacked any sort of solid character, at one point Callum wants to kill this guy she knew from school but then while fucking her after describes a fantasy of this dude joining? Very out of character, especially with how protective and possessive and obsessive he has been. Which is also another issue, after the first time they hooked up he was icky. He was predatory in not a hot way and whiny. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eOther issues: the villian, our god reads like a Scooby do character in this book. This entire thing was juvenile in nature. And I’m in shock because this is not like Harley’s other books. The pacing was so bad. The amount of unnecessary stuff was exhausting. By 50% which took me a full day and a half to get there (and I’m a fast reader) I began skimming. The entire time I felt the pregnancy plot coming, there were a dozen out of pocket comments and then 20 pages before the end we think her and the baby die and they don’t and then she’s all of a sudden become aware she is pregnant magically and is speaking to her belly. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eTriggers; as always Harley leaves a solid list of triggers but I want it to be known that one of them doesn’t even occur but it’s set up for us to think it occurs? \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eLike I said as my most anticipated read in two years I am fucking heart broken. This didn’t feel real. And I feel like I was robbed of an amazing set of characters and an amazing story that could have been. I know this is an unpopular opinion but my feelings be hurting.\u003cbr /\u003eI will make my notes public so you can see the things I am referring to. ","rating":1,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/AEILDFRP3W1EX\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.xGzgQB5fkrWMYEan\"}}"},"likeCount":32,"viewerHasLik